            <ArticleTitle>Eosinophillic myocarditis and coronary arteritis in a fatal case of asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>790-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0377-4929.72093</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mortality is very unusual in the case of asthma. We recently came across a fatal case of asthma which showed a rare combination of unusual complications like eosinophilic myocarditis, coronary arteritis, biventricular cardiac hypertrophy, eosinophilic pneumonitis and pulmonary hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
